Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide that covers everything from design to deployment.  
Feel free to skip sections that already exist in your project or to mix and match tools that fit your team’s skill set.

---

## 1. Planning & Design

| Step | What to do | Why it matters |
|------|------------|----------------|
| **Define goals** | List core features (product catalog, cart, checkout, search, filters, reviews, etc.). | Keeps scope focused. |
| **User personas** | Create 2–3 personas (e.g., “Budget shopper”, “Tech enthusiast”). | Drives UX decisions. |
| **Wireframes** | Sketch low‑fidelity screens (home, category, product, cart, checkout). | Visualise flow early. |
| **High‑fidelity mockups** | Use Figma/Sketch/Adobe XD. | Hand off to dev with pixel‑perfect specs. |
| **Design system** | Build a component library (buttons, cards, forms, icons). | Reusability & consistency. |
| **Accessibility audit** | Check contrast, keyboard navigation, ARIA labels. | Inclusive design & SEO. |

> **Tip:** Keep a shared Figma file for designers and developers; use “Design Tokens” for colors, spacing, typography.

---

## 2. Tech Stack Choices

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG) – great for SEO & performance. |
| **State** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, React Query | **React Query** for server state + **Redux Toolkit** for UI state. |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS, Styled‑Components, Emotion, CSS Modules | **Tailwind** + **CSS Modules** for rapid prototyping + scoped styles. |
| **Type System** | TypeScript | **Yes** – catches bugs early. |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | Unit + E2E coverage. |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | Automate lint, test, build, deploy. |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages | **Vercel** (native Next.js support). |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly). |
| **Payment** | Stripe, PayPal, Braintree | **Stripe** (modern API, easy integration). |
| **Auth** | Auth0, Firebase Auth, NextAuth.js | **NextAuth.js** (works well with Next.js). |
| **CMS / Headless** | Contentful, Sanity, Strapi, GraphCMS | **Sanity** (real‑time editing + GROQ). |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Server‑side rendering → instant page loads & SEO.  
> • Static site generation for product pages → lightning‑fast.  
> • API routes for serverless functions (checkout, webhook handling).  

---

## 3. Folder Structure (Next.js + TypeScript)

```
/src
  /components          # UI components (Button, Card, Modal, etc.)
  /pages               # Next.js pages (index.tsx, /products/[slug].tsx)
  /app                 # (optional) Next.js 13 app router
  /hooks               # Custom hooks (useCart, useAuth, useProducts)
  /lib                 # API clients, utilities
  /styles              # Tailwind config, global.css
  /types               # TypeScript types (Product, User, CartItem)
  /utils               # Helpers (formatPrice, debounce)
  /assets              # Images, icons
  /tests               # Jest + RTL tests
  /cypress             # Cypress E2E tests
  /storybook           # Component stories
  /public              # Static assets
```

---

## 4. Core Components & Pages

### 4.1 Product Card (React + Tailwind)

```tsx
// src/components/ProductCard.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import Image from 'next/image';
import { Product } from '@/types';

export const ProductCard = ({ product }: { product: Product }) => (
  <div className="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
    <Link href={`/products/${product.slug}`}>
      <a>
        <Image
          src={product.image}
          alt={product.title}
          width={300}
          height={300}
          className="object-cover w-full h-48"
        />
        <div className="p-4">
          <h3 className="font-semibold text-lg truncate">{product.title}</h3>
          <p className="text-gray-600 mt-1">{product.category}</p>
          <p className="mt-2 font-bold text-indigo-600">${product.price.toFixed(2)}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </Link>
  </div>
);
```

### 4.2 Category Page (Static Generation)

```tsx
// src/pages/category/[slug].tsx
import { GetStaticPaths, GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { fetchCategories, fetchProductsByCategory } from '@/lib/api';
import { ProductCard } from '@/components/ProductCard';

export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  const categories = await fetchCategories();
  return {
    paths: categories.map(c => ({ params: { slug: c.slug } })),
    fallback: false,
  };
};

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async ({ params }) => {
  const products = await fetchProductsByCategory(params?.slug as string);
  return { props: { products } };
};

export default function CategoryPage({ products }) {
  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-4">
      {products.map(p => (
        <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 4.3 Cart Context (React Query + Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// src/hooks/useCart.ts
import { useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { addToCart, removeFromCart, clearCart } from '@/store/cartSlice';

export const useCart = () => {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();
  const cart = useSelector(state => state.cart.items);
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  const add = (item) => {
    dispatch(addToCart(item));
    queryClient.invalidateQueries(['cart']);
  };

  const remove = (id) => {
    dispatch(removeFromCart(id));
    queryClient.invalidateQueries(['cart']);
  };

  const clear = () => {
    dispatch(clearCart());
    queryClient.invalidateQueries(['cart']);
  };

  return { cart, add, remove, clear };
};
```

---

## 5. API Integration

### 5.1 Fetching Products (REST)

```ts
// src/lib/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
});

export const fetchProducts = async () => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/products');
  return data;
};

export const fetchProductBySlug = async (slug: string) => {
  const { data } = await api.get(`/products/${slug}`);
  return data;
};
```

### 5.2 Checkout (Stripe + Next.js API Route)

```ts
// src/pages/api/checkout.ts
import Stripe from 'stripe';
const stripe = new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!, { apiVersion: '2023-10-16' });

export default async function handler(req, res) {
  if (req.method !== 'POST') return res.status(405).end();

  const { items, email } = req.body;

  const line_items = items.map((i: any) => ({
    price_data: {
      currency: 'usd',
      product_data: { name: i.title },
      unit_amount: Math.round(i.price * 100),
    },
    quantity: i.quantity,
  }));

  const session = await stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
    payment_method_types: ['card'],
    line_items,
    mode: 'payment',
    customer_email: email,
    success_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/success`,
    cancel_url: `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/cart`,
  });

  res.json({ url: session.url });
}
```

---

## 6. Testing

### 6.1 Unit Test (Jest + React Testing Library)

```tsx
// src/components/__tests__/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ProductCard } from '../ProductCard';
import { Product } from '@/types';

const mockProduct: Product = {
  id: '1',
  title: 'Test Shirt',
  slug: 'test-shirt',
  image: '/test.jpg',
  price: 29.99,
  category: 'Apparel',
};

test('renders product card', () => {
  render(<ProductCard product={mockProduct} />);
  expect(screen.getByText(/Test Shirt/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$29\.99/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

### 6.2 E2E Test (Cypress)

```js
// cypress/integration/cart.spec.js
describe('Cart Flow', () => {
  it('adds item to cart and checks out', () => {
    cy.visit('/');
    cy.get('[data-testid="add-to-cart"]').first().click();
    cy.get('[data-testid="cart-count"]').should('contain', '1');
    cy.get('[data-testid="checkout-button"]').click();
    cy.url().should('include', '/checkout');
  });
});
```

---

## 7. Deployment & CI/CD

1. **GitHub Actions** – lint, test, build, deploy to Vercel.
2. **Vercel** – auto‑deploy on push to `main`.  
   ```yaml
   # .github/workflows/deploy.yml
   name: Deploy
   on:
     push:
       branches: [main]
   jobs:
     build-and-deploy:
       runs-on: ubuntu-latest
       steps:
         - uses: actions/checkout@v3
         - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
           with:
             node-version: '20'
         - run: npm ci
         - run: npm run lint
         - run: npm run test
         - run: npm run build
         - uses: amondnet/vercel-action@v20
           with:
             vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
             vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
             vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
   ```

3. **Environment Variables** – store secrets in Vercel dashboard (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, etc.).

---

## 8. Performance & SEO

| Technique | How to implement |
|-----------|------------------|
| **Image Optimization** | Use Next.js `<Image>` component. |
| **Code Splitting** | Automatic with Next.js. |
| **Lazy Loading** | `loading="lazy"` on images, dynamic imports for heavy components. |
| **Meta Tags** | `next/head` for title, description, Open Graph. |
| **Sitemap** | Generate at build time (`next-sitemap`). |
| **Robots.txt** | Static file in `/public`. |
| **Accessibility** | `aria-*` attributes, semantic HTML, `tabIndex`. |

---

## 9. Analytics & Monitoring

| Tool | Why |
|------|-----|
| **Plausible** | Lightweight, privacy‑friendly. |
| **Sentry** | Runtime error tracking. |
| **LogRocket** | Session replay (optional). |

---

## 10. Next Steps

1. **Prototype**: Build a minimal viable product (MVP) with a handful of products.  
2. **Iterate**: Add filters, search, reviews, wishlist.  
3. **Scale**: Use CDN for images, enable incremental static regeneration for new products.  
4. **Security**: Harden API routes, use HTTPS, sanitize inputs.  
5. **Compliance**: GDPR, PCI‑DSS for payments.  

---

### Quick Checklist

